# AWS CloudWatch Logging Setup with Terraform

This repository contains the Terraform configuration used by the Nautilus DevOps team to provision AWS CloudWatch logging infrastructure for application log management.

## Project Overview

The goal of this configuration is to create a dedicated AWS CloudWatch Log Group and Log Stream to capture application logs.

### Resources Provisioned

* **AWS CloudWatch Log Group:** `datacenter-log-group`
* **AWS CloudWatch Log Stream:** `datacenter-log-stream`

---

## File Structure

```text
/home/bob/terraform/
├── main.tf              # Primary Terraform configuration declaring CloudWatch resources
├── provider.tf          # AWS Provider configuration
├── terraform.tfstate    # Terraform state file trackings created resources
└── README.md            # Documentation
Configuration (main.tf)
Terraform
resource "aws_cloudwatch_log_group" "datacenter_log_group" {
  name = "datacenter-log-group"
}

resource "aws_cloudwatch_log_stream" "datacenter_log_stream" {
  name           = "datacenter-log-stream"
  log_group_name = aws_cloudwatch_log_group.datacenter_log_group.name
}
Deployment Instructions
Navigate to the Terraform working directory:

Bash
cd /home/bob/terraform
Initialize Terraform:
Initializes backend configuration and downloads required provider plugins (AWS Provider v5.x).

Bash
terraform init
Plan and Apply Infrastructure:
Applies the Terraform configuration to create the CloudWatch log group and log stream.

Bash
terraform apply -auto-approve
Verify Deployment:
Confirm that resources were created and managed by Terraform:

Bash
terraform show
Verification
Upon successful execution of terraform apply, inspect the state output to confirm the resource Amazon Resource Names (ARNs):

Log Group ARN: arn:aws:logs:<region>:<account_id>:log-group:datacenter-log-group

Log Stream ARN: arn:aws:logs:<region>:<account_id>:log-group:datacenter-log-group:log-stream:datacenter-log-stream
